# The annotated PTX `analyze` prints: every input line, each loop
# header's label line followed by its trip count, k5's tile loop
# ⌈param_2/8⌉ unbound and 32 with the record's K = 256, its dot loop 8.
# With the record's block shape, 64 threads, each block's annotation
# names the warps and lanes that run it, on its label's line or else on
# its first instruction's after its name; the path for K = 0 runs on no
# thread. A block's statements run 64 threads x 16 CTAs x its loops'
# trips times over the record's launch, per CTA without the grid, and
# per thread, symbolic, without the block shape. A memory operand gives
# its address, a loop's iteration k as iv = k - 1, and a global one's
# sectors per warp request, a shared one's wavefronts, and the fewest.
# The `.entry` line names what the counts take of the launch: the grid,
# the block shape and the parameters bound, none where none is given;
# then the shared memory each CTA declares, `As` and `Bs`, 2048 B; then
# the FLOPs and bytes its statements sum to at the counts' scale: over
# the record's launch 2·256³ FLOPs of the K loop and 192 per thread of
# the epilogue, per CTA, and per thread symbolic in K = param_2.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/k5/k5.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --ncu %fixtures/k5/k5.sm_89.256.ncu.json %fixtures/k5/k5.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=NCU "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --bind 0:M=256 --bind 1:N=256 --bind 2:K=256 --launch 64,1,1 %fixtures/k5/k5.sm_89.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=SHAPE "%s"
CHECK: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z20hgemm_2d_blocktilingILi64ELi64ELi8ELi8ELi8EEviiifPK6__halfS2_fPS0_( // shared memory 2,048 B/CTA | per thread: flops f32 (1024·⌈param_2/8⌉ + 192); global load (32·⌈param_2/8⌉ + 128) B, store 128 B; shared load 256·⌈param_2/8⌉ B, store 32·⌈param_2/8⌉ B; param load 40 B{{$}}
CHECK: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips ⌈param_2/8⌉ | under line 64 | exec ⌈param_2/8⌉/thread{{$}}
CHECK: {{^}}$L__BB0_3: // loop: trips 8 | under line 64 | exec 8·⌈param_2/8⌉/thread{{$}}
NCU: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z20hgemm_2d_blocktilingILi64ELi64ELi8ELi8ELi8EEviiifPK6__halfS2_fPS0_( // grid 4×4×1 | block 64×1×1 | param_0 = 256, param_1 = 256, param_2 = 256 | shared memory 2,048 B/CTA | per launch: flops f32 33,751,040; global load 1,179,648 B, store 131,072 B; shared load 8,388,608 B, store 1,048,576 B; param load 40,960 B{{$}}
NCU: {{^}}	ld.param.u32 	%r7, [_Z20hgemm_2d_blocktilingILi64ELi64ELi8ELi8ELi8EEviiifPK6__halfS2_fPS0__param_1]; // [<block 0>] warp * × lane * | exec 1,024/launch{{$}}
NCU: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips 32 | global per CTA: requested 65,536 B, unique 65,536 B, sectors 98,304–147,456 B | warp * × lane * | exec 32,768/launch{{$}}
NCU: {{^}}	ld.global.u16 	%rs1, [%rd15]; // global load [32768·%ctaid.y + 16·iv[$L__BB0_2] + 512·⌊%tid.x/8⌋ + 2·(%tid.x mod 8) + param_4] sectors/req 4–8 (ideal 2){{$}}
NCU: {{^}}	st.shared.u16 	[%r20], %rs1; // shared store [2·%tid.x + As] wavefronts/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
NCU: {{^}}$L__BB0_3: // loop: trips 8 | warp * × lane * | exec 262,144/launch{{$}}
NCU: {{^}}	ld.shared.u16 	%rs17, [%r110]; // shared load [2·iv[$L__BB0_3] + 128·⌊%tid.x/8⌋ + As] wavefronts/req 4 (ideal 1){{$}}
NCU: {{^}}	@%p2 bra 	$L__BB0_3;{{$}}
NCU: {{^}}	shl.b32 	%r117, %r7, 3; // [<block 4>] warp * × lane * | exec 32,768/launch{{$}}
NCU: {{^}}$L__BB0_5: // no thread{{$}}
NCU: {{^}}$L__BB0_6: // warp * × lane * | exec 1,024/launch{{$}}
SHAPE: {{^}}.visible .entry _Z20hgemm_2d_blocktilingILi64ELi64ELi8ELi8ELi8EEviiifPK6__halfS2_fPS0_( // block 64×1×1 | param_0 = 256, param_1 = 256, param_2 = 256 | shared memory 2,048 B/CTA | per CTA: flops f32 2,109,440; global load 73,728 B, store 8,192 B; shared load 524,288 B, store 65,536 B; param load 2,560 B{{$}}
SHAPE: {{^}}$L__BB0_2: // loop: trips 32 | global per CTA: requested 65,536 B, unique 65,536 B, sectors 98,304–147,456 B | warp * × lane * | exec 2,048/CTA{{$}}
SHAPE: {{^}}$L__BB0_3: // loop: trips 8 | warp * × lane * | exec 16,384/CTA{{$}}
